b_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6 stable\n\nI'm only able to test since the introduction of Storage Access Framework, but I find it likely that this is not a regression, or it at least spans across several versions.\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 10 (build 19044) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.1659) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 13.85 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn Windows and Linux, `position` is passed down as a negative number, according to documentation.\n\nOn Android (tested on Huawei TGR-W09), the seek direction is flipped, breaking my game. When I pass a positive number instead, it works as intended.\n\nAdditionally, it seems that this specific line is the root cause of the bug:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5ad8b27d8db0776700c2b08bf68fbea5e0a4680d/platform/android/java/lib/src/main/java/org/godotengine/godot/io/file/DataAccess.kt#L206\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\n# on a non-empty file\nfunc test(file: FileAccess) -> void:\n\tvar size := file.get_length()\n\tfile.seek_end(-1)\n\tvar pos := file.get_position()\n\tassert(pos < size, \"huh\")\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[seekbug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24925231/seekbug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_i